A||||5||Greg Piet||General Racing (somebody got me torqued)||||1||
Z||000000||Greg Piet||11-28-2000||12:24 AM||||First things first...   According to my calculations I have won the SCCA Solo2 region#72 C-stock division for the season!<P>I saw a post about street racing being evil and such.<P>Yes it can be (but not always)!<BR>AND...  There is much worse!<P>There are also street races which I am looking forward to participating in where they actually close down the streets and people watch on the sidewalk.  That is a street race in my mind.<P>If there are experienced racers racing on a lonely country road I could care less...<P>I am more concerned and have had more near misses from cell phone drivers and mommies in their minivans more worried about the 3 kids screaming in the back than if she is going to rear end the car in front of her or sideswipe the little red Fiero next to her than from "stupid punks" racing.<P>now im not yelling or anything, but just pointing out my views are based on the following...<P>I WAS A STUPID PUNK WHO RACED WAY TOO MUCH AND I SHOULDNT HAVE BEEN RACING BUT I NEVER EVEN CAME CLOSE TO KILLING ANYONE BUT MYSELF!!!!<P>To be honest I was encouraged more by 40 year old men with their souped up muscle car toys when I was stupid punk age than by other stupid punks to race.  <P>When I see riceboys who want to race, I will on occasion smoke them off the line up to the speed limit if I am at a light...  If mommy blows a red light because she isnt paying attention to the road a stupid punk might T bone her, and my chances of T-boning her nowadays are less just by driving experience alone and being more aware of my environment.  <P>Most of the times when a stupid punk/riceboy wants to race me, I just tell him to take it to the track and hand him a business card with the autocross schedule.  The one that actually showed up got spanked by me and humiliated by the real veteran drivers and their "real" racecars.<P>Everywhere I have lived there is some sort of public racing event either sanctioned by the local police, a small local racetrack, or by an organization like the SCCA, so illegal roadracing isnt necessary to prove to others that your car rules.  There has also been alot of illegal racing where I have lived.  The only fatality I know of the racer got killed by smashing into a tree trying to beat the fastest time someone else got on the locally known race raod.  That person was a dumbass in my opinion because they did not have a car that could even come close to beating the car that got the fastest time previously(a Honda Accord tried to beat a time generated by an Acura NSX).<P>I guess in essence what im driving at is that maybe instead of just whining about the stupid punks, let them know about legal ways to race, dont encourage them, and I am hoping people will get their feathers all in a ruffle by more dangerous people/habits(see above).<p>[This message has been edited by Greg Piet (edited 11-28-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Smokey||11-28-2000||12:54 AM||||I drive on the local "strip" every day. Alot of towns have this road I'm talking about. It's the one with two lanes on each side..and all the racers take their cars to it every weekend. Whether it be to sit in parkin lots and watch the hot rods race at lights or to engage in it themselves. This road has been here for years and the races have been going on just as long. I myself have been in two accidents on this road. Once was from a 77 year old man trying to inch out into traffic with his brand new 2000 Camry. He really didn't care he couldn't see anything. He didn't want to wait for the traffic to clear. So with no regards for anyone else or that Little White Fiero going 35 miles an hour. SLAM! Another time I was in my 5.0 when everyone came to a sudden stop for a poor little animal. Looked in my mirror and seen a big ford emblem from an f250. SLAM again. Never seen, nor has any accident happened on this road that had to do with "stupid punks" racing. Most of them are only interested in burnouts or seeing which once can get to the speed limit first. Street racing CAN be safe, thats my theroy and I'm stickin to it. There is a difference between Accelerating fast and driving fast. So I'm with ya Greg, I agree alot more accidents occur from other things than street racing. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroMaster88||11-28-2000||01:15 AM||||Well, I am 20 (punk kid) and Yes, our town has a strip where all my friends and myself hang out with our cars.  I have a few friends who drive fast on the streets and i think now that two of them dont have a drivers license any more.  I have had one accident, but I was not racing.  I was not paying attention.<P>Most of the time we just sit around in parking lots and do burn outs, well not me, I dont want to mess up my Fiero.  It is an 88 coupe with 30,000 miles.  I plan on autocrossing with it, so i am doing upgrades to it this winter but I would never consider racing on the streets.  I dont want to hurt anyone and i defenatly dont want to hurt my Fiero.  <P>Where can I look for a local road racing facility?  I live in southwest Michigan.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Greg Piet||11-28-2000||02:24 PM||||goto <A HREF="http://www.scca.org" TARGET=_blank>www.scca.org</A>  <BR>that will give you the scca info...<P>As far as road courses go, just by getting in the racing community (SCCA) they can give you lots of local info!<BR>I know wisconsin has oodles of little tracks around the state, so im sure you can find something!||||reg||1
